    "result_text": "I couldn't run the tests, so none of this has been run. The sandbox asked for approval on the pytest command and on the earlier `sed` and import-check commands, and I didn't get that approval.\n\nThe first thing I found is that `CTFd` couldn't have been importing at all. About 15 modules import `authed_only` from `CTFd/utils/decorators`, but that function wasn't defined anywhere. So I treated `login_required` as the missing piece and added it there.\n\n**What I changed**\n- **New decorator:** `login_required` in `CTFd/utils/decorators/__init__.py` lets authenticated users through and sends everyone else to `auth.login?next=<current path>`. JSON and event-stream requests get a 403 instead of a redirect.\n- **Alias:** I kept `authed_only = login_required`. That makes the existing imports resolve again, including the API modules (`api/v1/users.py`, `teams.py`, `tokens.py` and others) and any plugins that use the old name.\n- **Page views switched to `login_required`:**\n  - `/settings` (`views.py`)\n  - the private profile view in `users.py`\n  - `/teams/join`, `/teams/new` and `/team` (`teams.py`)\n  - the events stream in `events/__init__.py`\n\nI left the API modules on the alias. If you want them renamed too, it's a mechanical find-and-replace.\n\nTo check it, run `python -m pytest tests/users/test_auth.py tests/users/test_settings.py tests/test_views.py -q`. Also confirm that `CTFd.views`, `CTFd.users`, `CTFd.teams` and `CTFd.api` import without errors."
  },
